import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'stairs-dead-torch':('Out of light on a staircase','A Warrior with a burned-out torch stands on a down staircase at depth 30. The out-of-light routine queues the stair key (<) but falls through and reports "nothing done", so the think loop keeps queueing commands behind it — commands that would land on the new level after the stairs were taken. The corrected routine returns true.'),
 'lit':('Control: plenty of torch fuel','With 2000 turns of torch both versions leave the routine alone. The complete logs are byte-identical.'),
 'dead-no-stairs':('Control: out of light, no staircase','With a dead torch and no staircase underfoot both versions find nothing to do. The complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/stairreturn-230 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP light=','setup'),('DECISION ','decision'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  seq=re.search(r'sequence=(.*)',raw)
  entry['sequence']=seq[1].strip() if seq else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The out-of-light stair command was queued and then disowned</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native out-of-light routines</p><h1>The out-of-light stair command was queued and then disowned</h1><p>When the Borg is out of light and standing on a staircase, its routine queues the stair key (&lt;). But the branch fell through without returning, so the routine reported "nothing done" — and the think loop, believing nothing was queued, kept queueing more commands behind the stair key. Everything after &lt; would land on the new level after the stairs were taken. The correction returns true after queueing the stair command.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The situation</button><button data-step="1">The routine</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With a healthy torch and with a dead torch away from stairs, both versions behave identically — leave it alone, find nothing — with byte-identical logs, so the correction changes only the on-stairs case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior, depth 30, seed 1000, glowing constructed arena, the worn torch's fuel set per situation, spare torches and the recall scroll removed from the pack (recorded as a fixture intervention) so the wear-stuff and recall branches have nothing to act on. The production out-of-light routine runs directly; its queued keys are shown, not executed. This isolates the missing return, not full autonomous play.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/230">issue230</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function routineLabel(c){if(!c||!c.outcome)return'?';return c.outcome.acted?`Reports done (keys: ${c.outcome.keys})`:'Reports nothing done'}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Light radius ${d.setup?d.setup.light:'?'}, on stairs: ${d.setup?d.setup.onstairs:'?'}.`:`${routineLabel(d)}`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'The out-of-light routine decides whether to take the stairs.':'What the routine reports back.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?`Queued: ${d.sequence||'none'}`:'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='stairs-dead-torch'?'The original queues &lt; and then reports nothing done; the correction reports done and stops the loop.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
